# Template — `infra/deploy.sh` substitutes {{DOMAIN}} and installs this at
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile. Not consumed directly.
#
# Caddy handles the Let's Encrypt certificate and renewal automatically; the
# only job here is reverse-proxying to the API process on localhost. Caddy
# forwards X-Forwarded-For/Proto and the original Host header by default —
# nothing extra to configure. The API trusts its own explicit `PUBLIC_URL`
# config for anything that needs to know its real external address (the
# OAuth redirect_uri, its Host-header allowlist) rather than trying to
# infer it from what a proxy forwards — see `PUBLIC_URL`'s doc comment in
# `apps/api/src/config.ts` for why.

{{DOMAIN}} {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4319
}
